2026-07-08 11:39:36,499 | AGENT | TechnicalArchitect Agent answered: To address the client's requirements, we propose an architecture that leverages our expertise in cloud architecture, cybersecurity, and data engineering. Our solution will be based on a hybrid deployment model, utilizing SecNumCloud-type infrastructure to ensure high security and compliance with regulatory requirements.

Firstly, to achieve response times under 2 seconds (con37), we will design a scalable and performant architecture using containerization with Docker and Kubernetes (K8s). This will enable us to efficiently manage and orchestrate our application containers, ensuring rapid deployment and scaling as needed. Additionally, we will utilize our experience with inference servers such as vLLM and Ollama to optimize the performance of our AI/ML models.

To ensure high availability compatible with municipal services needs (con38), we will implement a highly available architecture using load balancers and auto-scaling groups. This will guarantee that our solution can handle varying workloads and maintain uptime, even in the event of hardware or software failures. Our monitoring tools, including Prometheus and Grafana, will provide real-time insights into system performance, enabling swift issue detection and resolution.

For integration with existing systems of information (con42), we will utilize our expertise in API integration, employing API gateways such as Kong to facilitate secure and controlled access to our solution. We will also leverage our experience with message brokers like Apache Kafka to enable seamless communication between different systems.

Regarding hosting on SecNumCloud-type infrastructure or equivalent (con46), we have prior experience deploying solutions on OVHcloud, Scaleway, and Outscale (SecNumCloud), which meets the client's requirements. Our solution will be designed to take advantage of the security features provided by these cloud providers, ensuring the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of sensitive data.

To balance performance, security, and cost, we will make the following trade-offs:

* We will prioritize the use of open-source technologies where possible, such as Kubernetes and Docker, to minimize licensing costs while maintaining high performance and security.
* To optimize costs, we will utilize our experience with quantization methods like INT8 and INT4 (GPTQ) to reduce the energetic consumption of our AI/ML models, contributing to a more environmentally friendly solution.
* We will ensure that our solution is designed with security in mind from the outset, incorporating our expertise in cybersecurity to protect against potential threats and maintain the trust of municipal services.

By proposing this architecture, we believe we can meet the client's technical constraints while providing a balanced and effective solution that addresses performance, security, and cost considerations.
